{1 Troubleshooting}

{2 Common Issues}

{3 "TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN not set"}

{b Solution}: Export the environment variable:
{[
export TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN="your-token-here"
]}

{3 "Name error: Unbound module Eio"}

{b Solution}: Add [eio_main] to your dune file:
{[
(executable
 (libraries eio_main ocaml_telegram_eio.telegram ocaml_telegram_eio.tg))
]}

{3 "SSL/TLS errors"}

{b Solution}: Install CA certificates:
{[
opam install ca-certs ca-certs-nss
]}

{3 "Bot doesn't respond"}

{b Check}:
- Token is correct
- Bot is not blocked by user
- Polling is running (no errors in console)
- Handler is matching the update correctly

Add debug output:
{[
Eio.traceln "Update received: %d" update.update_id;
]}

