{1 Security Best Practices}

{2 Token Management}

{b Never}:
- Commit tokens to git
- Share tokens publicly
- Use production tokens in tests

{b Always}:
- Use environment variables
- Add [.env] to [.gitignore]
- Rotate tokens if compromised

{2 Input Validation}

Always validate user input:

{[
let handle_command text =
  match text with
  | txt when String.length txt > 4096 ->
      Error "Message too long"
  | txt when txt = "" ->
      Error "Empty message"
  | txt ->
      Ok txt
]}

{2 Rate Limiting}

Respect Telegram's rate limits:

{[
(* The library handles rate limits automatically with retry logic *)
let* response = Api.call client request in
(* Will retry with exponential backoff on 429 Too Many Requests *)
]}

See {{!Telegram.Limits}Limits module} for rate limit documentation.
